{"name":"Honesty","hex":"#dfebe9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Honesty","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Honesty"}],"entries":[{"title":"Honesty","blocks":[{"text":"Honesty or truthfulness is a facet of moral character that connotes positive and virtuous attributes such as integrity, truthfulness, straightforwardness, along with the absence of lying, cheating, theft, etc. Honesty also involves being trustworthy, loyal, fair, and sincere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Diogenes_looking_for_a_man_-_attributed_to_JHW_Tischbein.jpg/330px-Diogenes_looking_for_a_man_-_attributed_to_JHW_Tischbein.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honesty","wikidata":"Q337349"},{"title":"Honesty (Billy Joel song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Honesty\" is a song by American singer-songwriter Billy Joel, released by Columbia Records as the third US single from his sixth studio album 52nd Street (1978) in 1979. \"Honesty\" was solely written by Joel, while production was handled by Phil Ramone. The song appears on the Dutch and Japanese editions of Greatest Hits Volume 2, replacing \"Don't Ask Me Why\" (1980)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a5/Honesty_single.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honesty_(Billy_Joel_song)","wikidata":"Q3288620"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/TaytayChurchjf4190_03.JPG/500px-TaytayChurchjf4190_03.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/TaytayChurchjf4190_03.JPG/1280px-TaytayChurchjf4190_03.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia